---------------------------
Why do we need a Data Dictionary?
Imagine you receive: 
Sales.csv
with
sale_id
cst_id
prd_id
qty
amt
dt
A new developer asks:
What does amt mean?

Is it:
Gross Sales?
Net Sales?
Discount?
Profit?
Tax-inclusive amount?

Without documentation, people start guessing.
That's Dangerous
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 WHAT is a DATA DICTIONARY?

A Data Dictionanry is documentation that describes the structure and meaning of data.
It typically contains:
Column Name
Data Type
Description
Business Meaning
Nullable?
Example
Source
Business Rule

| Column       | Data Type | Description                 | Nullable | Example    |
| ------------ | --------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ---------- |
| sale_id      | INT       | Unique sales transaction ID | No       | 10001      |
| customer_id  | INT       | Customer identifier         | No       | 501        |
| product_id   | INT       | Product identifier          | No       | 101        |
| sale_date    | DATE      | Date of sale                | No       | 2026-08-18 |
| quantity     | INT       | Units sold                  | No       | 5          |
| sales_amount | DECIMAL   | Net sales amount            | No       | 2500.00    |

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚀 A professional Data Dictionary should answer: 
What?
What does the column represent?

Why?
Why do we need it?

Where?
Which source system does it come from?

How?
How is it calculated?

Rules?
What validation/business rules apply?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

